+## Clyra premium output rules (non-negotiable)
+
+**Never mock UI.** The page must never render a fake screenshot of an app,
+browser window, device frame, dashboard, or editor. Every visual slot is
+either real imagery or a neutral image placeholder:
+`<div class="ph-img" data-label="…">` styled as a soft grey tile with the
+label centred — or an `<img>` with an honest placeholder service
+(`https://picsum.photos/seed/<slug>/1600/900` copied locally when the brief
+names a real subject). A phone mock, browser chrome mock, or fake chart is a
+failed deliverable.
+
+**Modern, premium design language.**
+- One accent colour per page (from the design system), used for at most one
+  primary action per section. No purple-to-blue gradients, no glowing
+  borders, no sparkles, no decorative blobs.
+- Type first: a clear heading scale (display / h2 / h3 / body / caption),
+  tight tracking on large type, sentence case everywhere, no all-caps
+  paragraph labels.
+- A consistent spacing rhythm (4/8/16/24/48), generous section whitespace,
+  and hairline separators instead of heavy cards. Border-radius stays in a
+  single family (8–14px); nothing pill-shaped.
+- Quiet surfaces: near-white background, one neutral panel tone, hairline
+  borders. Depth only where it communicates interactivity.
+- Subtle, purposeful motion: 200–400ms ease-out fades and rises on scroll
+  entry; no looping decorative animation. Respect
+  `prefers-reduced-motion`.
+- Every section must answer a real question for the visitor. Remove any
+  section that exists only to fill space.
